    "scope": "Make the staging /profile 'セッション情報を取得できません' failure diagnosable on real staging and structurally prevent any localhost fallback in staging/production. The user asked whether the app points at 127.0.0.1; the confirmed answer is NO (the app fallback port is 8787, 8888 appears nowhere in app code, and the server-side /me fetch resolves via the API_SERVICE service-binding). This spec adds (1) transport-target observability: include transportKind (service-binding|http) and baseHost in the server_fetch_failed log so the real-device log proves the app is not calling localhost and reveals the true HTTP status (410/5xx/transport), and (2) localhost fail-closed: when ENVIRONMENT is not one of the enum values (not explicitly injected) the implicit local fallback to localhost is forbidden (throw) in staging/production. No /me response shape, status taxonomy, D1 schema, or Google Form change. apps/api is untouched. Full root-cause remediation is deferred to unassigned tasks until the real cause is confirmed on staging.",
